From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:27:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 05/30] wifi: ath12k: skip unbound links when unwinding a
 hardware scan

- Avoid dereferencing a missing radio after vdev creation or recovery fails.
- Preserve the existing scan cleanup for links that still have a radio.

[mzak: picked from SuperTurtleDev/iceland-mainline-kernel-linux dac82478404d (iceland-7.3) for q91j, gains #19; subject reworded to the subsystem style; applies unchanged. The patch carries no Signed-off-by of its author; carried with its authorship]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
index 41459fb4f..0c6a29bb6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -5966,6 +5966,9 @@ int ath12k_mac_op_hw_scan(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 			if (!arvif)
 				continue;
 
+			if (!arvif->ar)
+				continue;
+
 			ar = arvif->ar;
 			if (ar->scan.arvif == arvif) {
 				wiphy_work_cancel(hw->wiphy, &ar->scan.vdev_clean_wk);
-- 
